{#- Once-per-suite mock-request-count helper (alef issue #443).

   Context variables (see src/e2e/codegen/mock_assertions/helper.rs for the full contract):
   - helper_name: function name
   - total_path: mock server's total-count endpoint path
   - one_path: mock server's single-key endpoint path

   Emits ONE private function (`defp`) using Erlang's built-in `:httpc` (the OTP `inets`
   application), never `Req`/`Finch`: this backend's mix.exs only declares those when the suite
   has HTTP or mock-server fixtures (`elixir/project.rs::render_mix_exs`), but a `mock.*`
   assertion can appear on a fixture that trips neither flag, so the helper cannot assume either
   is a declared dependency. `:inets`/`:httpc` ship with every Erlang/OTP install, so this adds no
   new mix dependency at all. `Application.ensure_all_started/1` is idempotent -- safe to call on
   every invocation even once already started. Callers build `path_and_query` from
   "{{ total_path }}?prefix=<p>" (mock.requests.total) or "{{ one_path }}?key=<k>"
   (mock.requests["<k>"]) -- see mock_assertions::model::MockQuery. Appended directly to the
   enclosing `ExUnit.Case` module body, so every `test` block in the file can call it directly.
#}

  defp {{ helper_name }}(base_url, path_and_query) do
    {:ok, _} = Application.ensure_all_started(:inets)
    url = String.to_charlist(base_url <> path_and_query)

    case :httpc.request(:get, {url, []}, [], []) do
      {:ok, result} ->
        {status_line, _headers, body} = result
        {_protocol, status, _reason} = status_line

        if status == 200 do
          body
          |> List.to_string()
          |> String.trim()
          |> String.to_integer()
        else
          raise "{{ helper_name }}: unexpected HTTP status #{status}"
        end

      {:error, reason} ->
        raise "{{ helper_name }}: request failed: #{inspect(reason)}"
    end
  end
